prompt:
Implement a 3D sliding puzzle game using Three.js. A duck is hidden among 9 animated boxes.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/BoxAnimated.glb and assets/Duck.glb;
(2) Create 8 box instances (numbered 1-8) arranged in a 3x3 grid, leaving one empty slot;
(3) The box numbered 5 contains the hidden Duck model (not visible);

[Puzzle Interaction]
(4) When a box adjacent to the empty slot is clicked, that box slides into the empty slot (0.3-second animation);
(5) Only boxes adjacent to the empty slot horizontally or vertically can move;
(6) While moving, the box plays the opening-and-closing animation from BoxAnimated;

[Solution Detection]
(7) The puzzle is complete when the 8 boxes are arranged in the order 1-8;
(8) After completion, box number 5 opens, the Duck rises out of it with an animation, and then performs a rotating showcase;

[Shuffle]
(9) Randomly shuffle the initial state by performing 30-50 legal moves;
(10) A "Shuffle Again" button (id="shuffleBtn");

[HUD Display]
(11) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Move count (id="moves")
  - Whether the puzzle is solved (id="solved", true/false)
  - Whether the duck has been revealed (id="duckRevealed")
  - Elapsed time (id="elapsed")

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean
  - moveCount: number
  - solved: boolean
  - duckRevealed: boolean
  - elapsed: number (seconds)
  - emptySlot: {row, col}

Output a standalone HTML file.
